1
00:00:01,175 --> 00:00:03,790
Picture someone browsing a fashion store online.

2
00:00:04,148 --> 00:00:09,175
They find a dress, a jacket, or a linen shirt they love. The photographs look

3
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:10,108
beautiful.

4
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:11,968
But one question remains.

5
00:00:12,491 --> 00:00:14,673
What could this actually look like on me?

6
00:00:15,152 --> 00:00:21,064
GRINDCTRL's AI Virtual Try-On brings that moment closer to a personal shopping experience.

7
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:25,406
On a supported Shopify product page, the shopper selects an item.

8
00:00:25,685 --> 00:00:27,705
Taps try it on with AI.

9
00:00:27,883 --> 00:00:28,974
and uploads a photo.

10
00:00:31,413 --> 00:00:36,199
The system generates a visual preview of that shopper wearing the selected garment.

11
00:00:36,658 --> 00:00:38,877
It's important to understand what this means.

12
00:00:39,296 --> 00:00:42,056
The preview helps someone explore a style.

13
00:00:42,414 --> 00:00:45,510
It isn't an exact measurement, a fit guarantee.

14
00:00:45,646 --> 00:00:48,377
or a replacement for real product information.

15
00:00:50,834 --> 00:00:52,705
Now the shopper has another question.

16
00:00:53,064 --> 00:00:54,824
Does the shirt run oversized?

17
00:00:55,164 --> 00:00:56,375
Is there a size guide?

18
00:00:56,634 --> 00:00:58,190
What is the delivery policy?

19
00:00:58,649 --> 00:01:01,924
This is where Store Chat enters the same shopping journey.

20
00:01:02,343 --> 00:01:05,766
Instead of leaving the product page and searching across the website,

21
00:01:05,964 --> 00:01:08,020
The shopper opens the store assistant.

22
00:01:08,458 --> 00:01:13,514
Store Chat answers in English or Arabic using the information the merchant has supplied.

23
00:01:13,913 --> 00:01:16,115
Accurate answers come from store knowledge.

24
00:01:16,334 --> 00:01:18,835
not from made-up stock levels or promises.

25
00:01:19,256 --> 00:01:20,615
If human help is needed,

26
00:01:20,734 --> 00:01:22,891
the AI hands off with a reason.

27
00:01:23,189 --> 00:01:28,504
The team picks up the conversation in a shared inbox. Assigns it. adds a private note.

28
00:01:28,643 --> 00:01:30,337
and replies in context.

29
00:01:32,715 --> 00:01:35,111
Where appropriately configured and verified.

30
00:01:35,329 --> 00:01:39,007
Read-only order information can also support relevant questions.

31
00:01:39,325 --> 00:01:42,699
But the assistant shouldn't change orders. Promise refunds...

32
00:01:42,976 --> 00:01:46,437
or imply an integration exists when it hasn't been enabled.

33
00:01:46,874 --> 00:01:48,423
Let's connect the experience.

34
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,289
A shopper sees a garment.

35
00:01:50,629 --> 00:01:52,209
previews it on their own photo.

36
00:01:52,690 --> 00:01:55,344
asks about the size and gets a helpful answer.

37
00:01:55,662 --> 00:01:57,197
If the question needs judgment,

38
00:01:57,495 --> 00:02:02,462
a real person continues from the conversation already started. for a fashion brand.

39
00:02:02,601 --> 00:02:05,033
The two tools belong to one journey.

40
00:02:05,351 --> 00:02:08,089
Virtual Try-On helps people picture the product.

41
00:02:08,468 --> 00:02:10,387
Store Chat helps them understand it.

42
00:02:10,747 --> 00:02:13,711
The merchant's team stays in control when it matters.

43
00:02:14,212 --> 00:02:16,108
See the live product experience.

44
00:02:16,365 --> 00:02:21,638
Explore the demo and discover how GRINDCTRL can fit your Shopify fashion store.

45
00:02:22,076 --> 00:02:22,906
GRINDCTRL.

46
00:02:23,307 --> 00:02:25,737
Let shoppers see it. Let them ask.
